From c31cd3e0491808adca07e610a2cc809b2d162192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:11:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Plugin API 1.5.0: property sections, LogicState preset
 keys, entity inspectors

Three editor content extensions. Fio provides the mechanism; a plugin or
built-in game layer provides the content.

* EditorAPI.register_property_section(label, factory, entity_type=None,
  expanded=False): a collapsible section at the end of the Properties tab,
  same factory(thing) contract as register_property_tab, built lazily the
  first time it is opened (plugins/integration.py).
* EditorAPI.register_kv_suggestions(provider): provider(store) returns
  (label, key, default[, tooltip]) rows for the LogicState being edited; the
  panel shows a "Preset key" picker whose Insert adds a typed designer
  default, or selects the key if present (editor/property_editor.py).
* EditorAPI.register_entity_inspector(provider, entity_type=None):
  provider(entity, logic) returns an inspection document drawn by the new
  Entity Inspector (editor/entity_inspector.py), a live read-only panel
  opened from the Scene Hierarchy's Inspect action or
  MainWindow.show_entity_inspector(entity). With no provider it lists the
  entity's public properties.

Like the 1.4.0 Tools actions, each registration is recorded with its plugin
and drops out while that plugin is disabled. The change is additive: 1.4.0
plugins load and behave unchanged, and a plugin needing 1.6.0 is refused.

Two guard tests are updated, deliberately: test_keyvalue_group_is_generic
banned any suggestion hook in the property editor (to keep a game-specific
copy out of Fio); it now asserts the hook reaches the editor only through
the plugin manager and the editor carries no keys or game vocabulary of its
own. test_manager_has_no_rpg_inspector_provider still bans the old
game-side names and now names the generic hook it allows.

Full suite: 3958 passed, 5 skipped (opt-in benchmarks).

